There are many mosaics in the Hagia Sofia, most of them come from well after the classical period, having been created just after the periods of Byzantine Iconoclasm. Interestingly, one of these mosaics shows the Virgin Mary being presented with the city of Constantinople by Emperor Constantine and the Hagia Sofia itself by Emperor Justinian I. Very interesting artistic interpretation of the late Classical period originating from the height of the Byzantine Empire. Sadly, this is not classical, and therefore it is not the solution you are looking for.